0..76 Comment "/// This source states dependent cases over the 2-sphere into a path family."
77..147 Comment "/// The family stands in a sort with a loop and a 2-cell at one point."
148..151 Comment "///"
152..228 Comment "/// A case with no arm at the sphere\'s cell owes the transport of its answer"
229..304 Comment "/// along the cell. The family carries the answer along the bound path. Its"
305..382 Comment "/// image of the cell conjugates the answer by the images of the family\'s two"
383..459 Comment "/// endpoints. Where both images are empty, the answer moves to itself, also"
460..537 Comment "/// when it holds a loop. Where the images are one cell, reflexivity moves to"
538..590 Comment "/// the cell\'s inverse, then the cell, which cancel."
591..594 Comment "///"
595..670 Comment "/// A loop past an image that holds a cell whiskers the cell. The loops act"
671..745 Comment "/// freely on the cells, so no rule identifies the whiskered cell with the"
746..780 Comment "/// cell, and the case is refused."
781..784 Comment "///"
785..857 Comment "/// Limits: a nested carried transport carries reflexivity alone. A loop"
858..933 Comment "/// moves only past images that are empty by their syntax. Such an endpoint"
934..1013 Comment "/// never reads the binder or is one call whose case writes no arm at the cell."
1014..1017 Comment "///"
1018..1074 Comment "/// - see: #6458 — the reading of a family at the cell"
1075..1120 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/sphere.gandr"
1121..1171 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/sphere-maps.gandr"
1173..1189 Comment "// The 2-sphere."
